 ["6–16 May 1982", "Westerly wind burst documented from 12-hourly island, atoll and ship reports: 11 days, within about 5° of the equator, growing from about 1000 km to over 3500 km in zonal extent; strongest over 135°–155°E. OLR-based indices show an active MJO (OMI phases 6–7, up to 2.3; convection at 80°E on 21–27 Apr, then 150°E by 9 May), but BoM RMM is only 0.6–1.2 during the burst.", "Authors attribute the burst to a midlatitude-forced pressure rise in the far western equatorial Pacific, prolonged by a pressure fall near 150°–160°E; they describe it as the first sustained burst of 1982, about three months before onset.", c('chufrederick1990', 'psl'), "High (wind event); Low (contribution)"],
